== the three content sets, on P1.2 and P2.2 ==
# ASCII is the manifest's set. LATIN1 is one code point per character in U+00A0 to
# U+00FF, which a JVM String still stores compactly. Above U+00FF is U+4E00 and up,
# inside the BMP so still one char per code point, and it is where a JVM String
# becomes UTF16 -- so the binding stages twice the bytes and the core runs a
# different transcoder.

### content set 0, P1.2
content set: ASCII (design/SHAPES.md's default; every id in the real schema is an ASCII GUID)
id     bytes    base ns/op  pbj-reused-out        pbj-parsed            pbj-loop              pbj-reuse             pbj-det               R                     ffi                   ffi-nobatch           ffi-zeroed            R-take                ffi-take              
