### content set 1, P1.2
content set: LATIN1 but not ASCII -- one code point per input character, U+00A0 to U+00FF. On the JVM this is still the compact coder, so the target's fast path applies and the CORE's transcoder changes from latin1 to latin1 with two-byte output
id     bytes    base ns/op  pbj-reused-out        pbj-parsed            pbj-loop              pbj-reuse             pbj-det               R                     ffi                   ffi-nobatch           ffi-zeroed            R-take                ffi-take              
